<p>Venezuela’s National Assembly unanimously approved an organic mining law on April 9, opening the sector to private and foreign investment in a notable policy shift as the government tries to bring capital into the country’s mineral industry. The bill sets a new legal framework for mining and now heads to constitutional review before it can fully take effect. Officials cast the measure as part of broader economic changes meant to increase foreign participation in natural resource industries.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/2BAjrCD_55E59ACwS9lJwDK-VekOAvM1W_dJEzGIZ89aokJ2Pj6WHrcw22k1_At0RuFgRv7FI9tAxSe1DvOZg0BHPk4sBSU-OLp5ulEQqXkbjGgjn4rTn7vJ4k47-E36jphE_kaLofwpXPg4HZPPVtD-NjB7fKHoRdqYRbSSqcNdljPKCqtVRaJ8N6g9IdEFg5CD7iq4AdCtR4qRNkHXpDK-6kuKIN7v4UX1WYtG3CF8U8vnj8OQ1kKHIUE' alt='Venezuela&#x27;s National Assembly discuss a new mining law expected to open the sector to private and foreign investment, in Caracas, Venezuela, March 9, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Investor safeguards: The bill includes independent arbitration because foreign investors see outside dispute resolution as an important safeguard against the risk of government asset seizures in Venezuela.</li><li>State messaging: After lawmakers approved the bill, National Assembly president Jorge Rodriguez said it would help build future prosperity while protecting mining workers.</li><li>Sector risks: ABC reported that Venezuela’s once-private mining industry has long been exploited by criminal groups with ties to the government, highlighting the governance challenge facing any new investment.</li><li>Labor unrest: The parliamentary vote came as thousands of workers marched for a higher minimum wage after it had been frozen since 2022, with Mercopress reporting police repression of the demonstrations.</li></ul><blockquote>vehicle for the construction of future prosperity - Jorge Rodriguez</blockquote><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/09/world/americas/venezuela-mining-us.html'>Venezuela Approves New Law to Open Mining to Foreign Investors</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/10/venezuelan-lawmakers-approve-sweeping-mining-bill-to-lure-foreign-investors_6752277_4.html'>Venezuelan lawmakers approve sweeping mining bill to lure foreign investors</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/04/10/venezuelan-parliament-passes-law-opening-mining-sector-to-private-capital-amid-rapprochement-with-us'>Venezuelan parliament passes law opening mining sector to private capital amid rapprochement with US</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/venezuelan-lawmakers-approve-sweeping-mining-bill-lure-foreign-131895887'>Venezuelan lawmakers approve a sweeping mining bill to lure foreign investors</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/venezuelan-lawmakers-approve-sweeping-mining-bill-to-entice-wary-foreign-investors'>Venezuelan lawmakers approve sweeping mining bill to entice wary foreign investors</a> - pbs.org</li></ul>